diff:1203726672:1203542844:=1,392c1%0a%3c Para o funcionamento do LTSP, é preciso alguns programas.\\%0a%3c '''#apt-get install dhcp3-server tftpd-hpa portmap nfs-kernel-server'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c ltsp-utils, com ele instala e configura o ltsp.\\%0a%3c '''#apt-get install ltsp-utils'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Sobre Instalando a partir da .ISO\\%0a%3c http://wiki.ltsp.org/twiki/bin/view/Ltsp/LTSP-42#Installing_from_the_LTSP_4_2u2_I\\%0a%3c Obter a .iso\\%0a%3c http://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/isos/%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Montar .Iso do LTSP4.2\\%0a%3c '''#mount -o loop ltsp-4.2u2-0.iso /mnt'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Abra o '''#ltspadmin'''%0a%3c http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/anexo/ltspadmin_conf_install.png%0a%3c Na tela do ltspadmin vamos primeiro em '''Configure the installer options'''%0a%3c %0a%3c Em '''Where to retrieve packages from?''' vamos trocar e colocar:\\%0a%3c '''[=file:///mnt/=]'''%0a%3c %0a%3c na opção abaixo '''In which directory would you like to place the LTSP client tree?\\%0a%3c [/opt/ltsp]'''\\%0a%3c Indicado manter o padrão e pra outras pode deixar em branco e dar enter.%0a%3c http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/anexo/ltspadmin_conf_install-feito.png%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Para instalar vamos em '''Install/Update LTSP Packages'''\\%0a%3c Tecle '''A''' para selecionar todos arquivos para instalação\\%0a%3c e '''Q''' para começar o Download\\%0a%3c Instalou e tecle '''Enter''' para continuar%0a%3c %0a%3c ----%0a%3c %0a%3c Com LTSP já instalado, falta somente configurar...\\%0a%3c mas antes vamos editar/verificar se alguns arquivos estão como devem.%0a%3c %0a%3c Abra o:\\%0a%3c '''#nano /etc/default/tftpd-hpa'''\\%0a%3c (pode usar seu editor preferido...vi, vim, pico, emacs e etc...)%0a%3c %0a%3c E deixe o arquivo '''tftpd-hpa''' deste jeito...%0a%3c [@%0a%3c #Defaults for tftpd-hpa%0a%3c RUN_DAEMON="yes"%0a%3c OPTIONS="-l -s /tftpboot"%0a%3c @]%0a%3c Salva e pronto.%0a%3c %0a%3c O servidor deve ter duas placas de rede, vamos usar aqui no exemplo a eth1 com ip 192.168.20.1 para o LTSP\\%0a%3c Para isso vamos abrir o:\\%0a%3c '''#nano /etc/network/interfaces'''\\%0a%3c E colocar a seguinte configuração na eth1 deste jeito.%0a%3c [@auto eth1%0a%3c iface eth1 inet static%0a%3c         address   192.168.20.1%0a%3c         netmask   255.255.255.0%0a%3c         network   192.168.20.0%0a%3c         broadcast 192.168.20.255@]%0a%3c depois executar...\\%0a%3c '''#/etc/init.d/networking restart'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Para ver como esta a configuração atual do LTSP\\%0a%3c '''#ltspcfg'''\\%0a%3c tecle '''S''' e veja se tem tudo instalado%0a%3c %0a%3c Maiores informações:\\%0a%3c 2.5. Exibindo a configuração atual\\%0a%3c http://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/docs/ltsp-4.1-ptbr.html#AEN641%0a%3c %0a%3c ----%0a%3c %0a%3c Em '''#ltspcfg''' Tecle '''C''' (configure)\\%0a%3c 2.3. Configurando os serviços necessários ao LTSP\\%0a%3c http://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/docs/ltsp-4.1-ptbr.html#AEN443%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c '''Vamos Configurar'''\\%0a%3c http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/anexo/ltspcfg-c.png%0a%3c %0a%3c '''1 - Runlevel'''\\%0a%3c e mude o Runlevel para '''5'''%0a%3c %0a%3c '''2 - Interface selection'''\\%0a%3c e escolha a interface/placa de rede que LTSP vai usar.\\%0a%3c Vamos aqui usar a '''eth1''' que antes já configuramos%0a%3c %0a%3c '''3 - DHCP configuration'''\\%0a%3c aqui criei o arquivo dhcpd.conf\\%0a%3c Do you want to build a dhcpd.conf file (y/n) ? '''Y'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c em outro Terminal/Aba faça\\%0a%3c '''#mv /etc/dhcp3/dhcpd.conf.sample /etc/dhcp3/dhcpd.conf'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c E agora edite o dhcpd.conf\\%0a%3c '''#nano /etc/dhcp3/dhcpd.conf'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c e procure por:%0a%3c [@%0a%3c option domain-name            "your_domain.org";   # You really should fix this%0a%3c @]%0a%3c e coloque o domínio da sua rede.\\%0a%3c Sugestão usar "ltsp"%0a%3c [@%0a%3c option domain-name            "ltsp";   # You really should fix this%0a%3c @]%0a%3c procure a linha - subnet 192.168.0.0 netmask 255.255.255.0%0a%3c [@%0a%3c  subnet 192.168.0.0 netmask 255.255.255.0 {%0a%3c  range 192.168.0.100 192.168.0.199;%0a%3c  if substring (option vendor-class-identifier, 0, 9) = "PXEClient" {%0a%3c  filename "/lts/2.6.16.1-ltsp-1/pxelinux.0";%0a%3c  }%0a%3c  else{%0a%3c  filename "/lts/vmlinuz-2.6.16.1-ltsp-1";%0a%3c  }%0a%3c  }%0a%3c @]%0a%3c Verifica se esta com o ip de sua rede configurada na eth1.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Em um Terminal/Aba execute: '''ls /tftpboot/lts''' e veja o retorno.%0a%3c [@%0a%3c # ls /tftpboot/lts%0a%3c  2.6.17.3-ltsp-1 vmlinuz-2.6.17.3-ltsp-1%0a%3c @]%0a%3c No dhcpd.conf criado esta escrito a versão - 2.6.16.1-ltsp-1 - só que ltsp tem instalado a: 2.6.'''17.3'''-ltsp-1.\\%0a%3c Mude para '''2.6.17.3-ltsp-1'''.%0a%3c %0a%3c Agora faça as mudanças no '''option domain-name''', '''subnet''' e no '''filename''' -, o dhcp.conf deve ficar assim.%0a%3c [@%0a%3c # dhcpd.conf%0a%3c %0a%3c  ddns-update-style ad-hoc;%0a%3c %0a%3c  option subnet-mask 255.255.255.0;%0a%3c  option broadcast-address 192.168.20.255;%0a%3c  option routers 192.168.20.1;%0a%3c  option domain-name-servers 192.168.20.1;%0a%3c  option domain-name "ltsp"; # You really should fix this%0a%3c  option option-128 code 128 = string;%0a%3c  option option-129 code 129 = text;%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c  get-lease-hostnames true;%0a%3c %0a%3c  next-server 192.168.20.1;%0a%3c  option root-path "192.168.20.1:/opt/ltsp/i386";%0a%3c %0a%3c  subnet 192.168.20.0 netmask 255.255.255.0 {%0a%3c  range 192.168.20.100 192.168.20.110;%0a%3c  if substring (option vendor-class-identifier, 0, 9) = "PXEClient" {%0a%3c  filename "/lts/2.6.17.3-ltsp-1/pxelinux.0";%0a%3c  }%0a%3c  else{%0a%3c  filename "/lts/vmlinuz-2.6.17.3-ltsp-1";%0a%3c  }%0a%3c  }%0a%3c #%0a%3c # If you need to pass parameters on the kernel command line, you can%0a%3c # do it with option-129. In order for Etherboot to look at option-129,%0a%3c # you MUST have option-128 set to a specific value. The value is a%0a%3c # special Etherboot signature of 'e4:45:74:68:00:00'.%0a%3c #%0a%3c # Add these two lines to the host entry that needs kernel parameters%0a%3c #%0a%3c # option option-128 e4:45:74:68:00:00; # NOT a mac address%0a%3c # option option-129 "NIC=ne IO=0x300";%0a%3c #%0a%3c @]%0a%3c Feito tudo...execute.\\%0a%3c '''#/etc/init.d/dhcp3-server restart'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Voltar ao Terminal/Aba que tem o Menu de Configure%0a%3c %0a%3c '''4 - TFTP configuration'''\\%0a%3c coloque **Y** (yes ) para ligar/enabled o TFTP%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Na instalação que fiz tive o seguinte mensagem de retorno, quando tentei ligar o TFTP\\%0a%3c '''The signal has been sent to start tftpd, but it doesn't appear to be running'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c e tentei dar um restart no inetd - #/etc/init.d/inetd restart - mas o arquivo não existia.\\%0a%3c Solução foi continuar a instalação, e assim que terminar reiniciar o PC. %0a%3c %0a%3c '''Em instalações mais recentes com Debian Etch este erro não tem aparecido. O TFTP é ativado corretamente. (11/05/2007)'''%0a%3c %0a%3c Em outro Terminal/Aba antes edite:\\%0a%3c '''#nano /etc/inetd.conf'''\\%0a%3c e procure pela linha.%0a%3c [@%0a%3c #:BOOT: Tftp service is provided primarily for booting.  Most sites%0a%3c # run this only on machines acting as "boot servers."%0a%3c tftp           dgram   udp     wait    root  /usr/sbin/in.tftpd /usr/sbin/in.tftpd -s /tftpboot%0a%3c %0a%3c @]%0a%3c e deixe como esta acima. ...'''-s /tftpboot'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Bem continuando a instalação....%0a%3c %0a%3c '''5 - Portmapper configuration'''\\%0a%3c coloque '''Y''' (yes) para ligar/enabled.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c '''6 - NFS configuration'''\\%0a%3c coloque '''Y''' (yes) para ligar/enabled.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c '''7 - XDMCP configuration'''\\%0a%3c coloque '''Y''' (yes) para ligar/enabled.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c 8 - Create /etc/hosts entries\\%0a%3c 9 - Create /etc/hosts.allow entries\\%0a%3c 10 - Create /etc/exports entries\\%0a%3c 11 - Create lts.conf file\\%0a%3c Nesta 4 seleções coloque '''Y (yes)''' para que o '''ltspcfg''' criar as entradas de configurações em cada arquivo e crie o arquivo '''lts.conf'''\\%0a%3c Abaixo vamos editar algumas configurações que '''ltspcfg''' criou.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c '''8 - Create /etc/hosts entries'''\\%0a%3c Se o arquivo '''#cat /etc/hosts''' - tiver como retorno um parecido com abaixo%0a%3c [@%0a%3c ## LTSP-begin ##%0a%3c #%0a%3c # The lines between 'LTSP-begin' and 'LTSP-end' were added%0a%3c # on: Qua Abr 18 23:55:07 2007, by the ltspcfg configuration tool.%0a%3c # For more information, visit the LTSP homepage%0a%3c # at http://www.LTSP.org%0a%3c #%0a%3c %0a%3c ......%0a%3c 192.168.20.84           ws084.ltsp      ws084%0a%3c 192.168.20.85           ws085.ltsp      ws085%0a%3c 192.168.20.86           ws086.ltsp      ws086%0a%3c 192.168.20.87           ws087.ltsp      ws087%0a%3c ......%0a%3c %0a%3c @]%0a%3c esta tudo ok%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c '''9 - Create /etc/hosts.allow entries'''\\%0a%3c Edite o arquivo '''#nano /etc/hosts.allow'''%0a%3c [@%0a%3c bootpd:     0.0.0.0%0a%3c in.tftpd:   192.168.20.0%0a%3c portmap:    192.168.20.0%0a%3c @]%0a%3c %0a%3c mude para ip que tu tem configurado no seu servidor. No caso aqui: '''192.168.20.1'''%0a%3c [@%0a%3c bootpd:     0.0.0.0%0a%3c in.tftpd:   192.168.20.1%0a%3c portmap:    192.168.20.1%0a%3c @]%0a%3c Salve e pronto.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c '''10 - Create /etc/exports entries'''\\%0a%3c Edite o arquivo '''#nano /etc/exports''' - mudando para o ip do servidor. Deve ficar assim:%0a%3c [@%0a%3c ## LTSP-begin ##%0a%3c #%0a%3c # The lines between 'LTSP-begin' and 'LTSP-end' were added%0a%3c # on: Qua Abr 18 23:57:57 2007, by the ltspcfg configuration tool.%0a%3c # For more information, visit the LTSP homepage%0a%3c # at http://www.LTSP.org%0a%3c #%0a%3c %0a%3c /opt/ltsp                 192.168.20.1/255.255.255.0(ro,no_root_squash,sync)%0a%3c /var/opt/ltsp/swapfiles   192.168.20.1/255.255.255.0(rw,no_root_squash,async)%0a%3c %0a%3c ## LTSP-end ##%0a%3c @]%0a%3c Pronto....reinicie a maquina e faça os teste nos terminais.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Pelo problema no inetd foi preciso eu reiniciar...mas depois eu fui em '''ltspcfg''' e fui ver o '''S''' Status (ou '''#ltspcfg -p''') e estava o TFTP rodando e nos terminais funcionou.%0a%3c [@%0a%3c Interface IP Address      Netmask         Network         Broadcast        Used%0a%3c eth0      xxx.xx.xxx.xxx  255.255.252.0   xxx.xx.xxx.x    255.255.255.255%0a%3c eth1      192.168.20.1    255.255.255.0   192.168.20.0    192.168.20.255  %3c-----%0a%3c %0a%3c Service    Installed   Enabled   Running   Notes%0a%3c dhcpd      Yes         Yes       Yes       Version 3%0a%3c tftpd      Yes         Yes       Yes       Has '-s' flag%0a%3c portmapper Yes         Yes       Yes%0a%3c nfs        Yes         Yes       Yes%0a%3c xdmcp      Yes         Yes       Yes       gdm   Using: gdm%0a%3c %0a%3c File                                Configured  Notes%0a%3c /etc/hosts                          Yes%0a%3c /etc/hosts.allow                    Yes%0a%3c /etc/exports                        Yes%0a%3c /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/lts.conf         Yes%0a%3c %0a%3c Configured runlevel: 5         (value of initdefault in /etc/inittab)%0a%3c    Current runlevel: 5         (output of the 'runlevel' command)%0a%3c %0a%3c Installation dir...: /opt/ltsp%0a%3c %0a%3c Press %3center> to return to the main menu...%0a%3c @]%0a%3c %0a%3c Maiores Informações de Instalação no Debian e exemplos de arquivo de configuração.\\%0a%3c http://www.ltsp-br.org/wiki2/doku.php?id=debian\\%0a%3c http://oca.idbrasil.org.br/wiki2/index.php/Instala%25C3%25A7%25C3%25A3o_LTSP_4.2\\%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c ----%0a%3c %0a%3c Logs da Conversa\\%0a%3c '''Log1''' [[http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/anexo/log-gtalk-ltsp-br-19-04.txt|log-gtalk-ltsp-br-19-04.txt]]\\%0a%3c '''Log2''' [[http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/anexo/log-irc-ltsp-br-19-04.txt|log-irc-ltsp-br-19-04.txt]]\\%0a%3c '''Log3''' [[http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/anexo/log-irc-ltsp-br-20-04.txt|log-irc-ltsp-br-20-04.txt]]\\%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c e-mails para listas\\%0a%3c debian etch (ltsp4.2u2 ou ltsp5.0 ou via aptitude install ltsp-utils)\\%0a%3c http://listas.cipsga.org.br/pipermail/ltsp-br-discuss/2007-April/000151.html\\%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Erro no dhcpd.conf\\%0a%3c http://listas.cipsga.org.br/pipermail/ltsp-br-discuss/2007-April/000162.html\\%0a%3c http://lists.debian.org/debian-user-portuguese/2007/04/msg01092.html\\%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c erro no boot via disquete (tftp erro - file not found)\\%0a%3c http://listas.cipsga.org.br/pipermail/ltsp-br-discuss/2007-April/000169.html\\%0a%3c http://listas.cipsga.org.br/pipermail/ltsp-br-discuss/2007-April/000170.html\\%0a%3c http://listas.cipsga.org.br/pipermail/ltsp-br-discuss/2007-April/000191.html\\%0a%3c (solução final com Lucas no IRC - log3)%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Saber o Modelo da Placa de Rede\\%0a%3c '''#lspci -n'''%0a%3c [@%0a%3c 00:00.0 0600: 1039:0648 (rev 51)%0a%3c 00:01.0 0604: 1039:0003%0a%3c 00:02.0 0601: 1039:0963 (rev 25)%0a%3c 00:02.1 0c05: 1039:0016%0a%3c 00:02.5 0101: 1039:5513%0a%3c 00:02.7 0401: 1039:7012 (rev a0)%0a%3c 00:03.0 0c03: 1039:7001 (rev 0f)%0a%3c 00:03.1 0c03: 1039:7001 (rev 0f)%0a%3c 00:03.3 0c03: 1039:7002%0a%3c 00:0b.0 0200: 10ec:8139 (rev 10)%0a%3c 00:0c.0 0200: 1106:3106 (rev 86)%0a%3c 01:00.0 0300: 10de:0322 (rev a1)%0a%3c @]%0a%3c desta retorno usar somente as linhas que tem **0200**\\%0a%3c [@%0a%3c 00:0b.0 0200: 10ec:8139 (rev 10)%0a%3c 00:0c.0 0200: 1106:3106 (rev 86)%0a%3c @]%0a%3c '''#lspci -n | grep "Class 0200"'''\\%0a%3c lista somente as linhas que tem '''0200'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Saber o MAC addresses\\%0a%3c '''#ifconfig'''%0a%3c [@%0a%3c eth0       Encapsulamento do Link: Ethernet  Endereço de HW 00:08:54:14:8D:AD%0a%3c           inet end.: 201.72.186.116  Bcast:255.255.255.255  Masc:255.255.252.0%0a%3c           endereço inet6: fe80::208:54ff:fe14:8dad/64 Escopo:Link%0a%3c           UP BROADCASTRUNNING MULTICAST  MTU:1500  Métrica:1%0a%3c           RX packets:1347710 errors:0 dropped